      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "From an actuarial standpoint, weighting this correlation requires building a time-series regression model that incorporates lagged demographic change variables against incident reports. Instead of a simple correlation, use a vector autoregression (VAR) model to test for leading indicators; for instance, rapid changes in renter-to-owner ratios combined with demographic shifts might be stronger predictors of instability than either factor alone. This allows you to quantify not just the correlation, but the dynamic pressure the shift exerts on the risk profile.",
      "source": "target",
